index=web sourcetype=access_combined
| rex field=_raw "\"\s+(?<http_status>\d{3})\s+"
| where http_status>=400
| stats count by http_status
| sort -count

I use this search to identify HTTP errors in Apache access logs.
First, I extract the HTTP status code. 
Then I filter for errors and count how many times each status occurs.
This helps me identify problems affecting the e-commerce website.
